      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Want to add to this, \n\nAs a DJ this has been a major limitation, Often when performing for a specific group, that group will make an instance in their name. Yet if I want to guide people to that event the only recourse I have with groups is to send out a group message for \"my\" group, instructing people to just join on me or find/join the other group and join that way instead.\n\nInitially I thought groups could help me a lot with reducing the rate I befriend random people at my DJ sets, as I could have them join via the group system.\n\nHowever to this day, when the event's instance is not \"mine\" the only way people can join an event where a DJ is performing is by befriending that DJ in advance and knowing to join on them when the event takes place.\n\nIt would be really nice if a Group instance could \"feature\" another group\n\n(or series of groups) that would allow a party instance to say:\n\n[PARTY GROUP] featuring [DJ GROUP]!\n\nThat will show the event in people's \"Active group list\" in their social list.\n\nOne thing to take note of is that Party's often feature multiple DJ's in rapid succession, so it would be good to allow the instance host (or someone with admin role in the hosting group) to switch out the \"featured\" performer group as soon as the featured artist changes (not requiring portalling to a new instance as that will always come with a user attendance penalty, not everyone jumps to the next instance)\n\n \n\nMulti-group features might also be an option which saves micro-managing for the hosting group, as they can just add the entire featured-groups list up front without worrying about change overs. One caveat to keep track of of \n\nwould be the potential for multiple groups to feature the same group during overlapping moments when an artist is double booked by two events that overlap with each other.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2022-12-03T03:14:38.865Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "when multiple groups collaborate it would be great to be able to have an instance that in owned by both. this way both group's members can see the instances and both group's instance moderators can preform their duties.\n\nbeyond this it would be nice to be able to dynamically change what groups own an instance for events where 1 group hosts multiple other groups at different times of the same event.",
